  "notes": [
    "Every hand that ends with one player left records a pot eligible to that player alone; that pot is genuine when it contains other (folded) players' money, which is why handsWithOnePlayerPot is close to hands.",
    "Single-contributor walks (PRE 21, POST 11, all tournament NLH, rake 0): only the big blind put chips in, so the engine's stated rule refunds nothing (nothing was called); the player's own chips come back through the pot. No chip effect; listed separately rather than as violations.",
    "2 POST walks have no one-player pot because short players were all-in on forced posts (multi-eligible pots); both refunded correctly.",
    "Pineapple discard actions are treated as moving no chips; no hand was excluded in either window.",
    "All 24 PRE violations are tournament walks with no small blind posted and individual antes (no rake, so no chip moved differently); none in cash. The 9 Omaha ones are the C-F1 hands of the classic artifact.",
